<Base title="Design system · U.S. Code">
  <h1 class="doc-title">Design system</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Every part the reader is built from, on one page, rendered by the same components the rest
    of the site renders. The type and the reading measure, the palette with its measured
    contrast, the focus ring, the status badges, the navigation chrome and the release switcher,
    the keyboard map, the version timeline and the redline, the statutory text with its copy
    control, the two reading densities, the print layout, a search result row with its facets,
    and each message the site can put in front of you.
  </p>

  <p>
    This page reaches no data. The provision it shows is a specimen under title 0, which the
    Office of the Law Revision Counsel does not publish: its citations and links resolve to
    nothing, and its words are not law.
  </p>

  <p class="doc-meta">
    The colour table computes itself from the tokens this page has resolved, so it is correct
    in whichever theme you are reading. Use the <strong>Dark</strong> control in the header to
    see the other one.
  </p>

