  {/* --------------------------------------------------------------- measure */}
  <h2 class="toc-group" id="measure">The reading measure</h2>

  <p>
    One token, <code>--measure</code>, sets the width of the reading column and of the chrome
    that spans it. It is a multiple of <code>--reading-size</code> rather than a fixed width, so
    the column narrows with the text and the line holds the same number of characters at either
    reading density. The block below is the reading column, bounded. Characters per rendered line are counted by
    <code>make measure</code> into <code>docs/verification/measure.json</code> rather than
    estimated from a glyph width: a median of 67, and 62 to 71 across the tenth and ninetieth
    percentiles, in both densities.
  </p>

  <div class="spec">
    <p class="spec__measure" data-measure-sample>
      The Secretary shall publish a specimen in the Federal Register not later than 30 days
      after the date of enactment of this section, and shall thereafter maintain it in a form
      that can be read at the width the reader was designed for rather than the width the
      window happens to be.
    </p>
    <p class="spec__meta">
      <code>--measure</code> resolves here to <span data-measure-token>—</span>, and the
      paragraph above is <span data-measure-width>—</span> wide at this viewport.
    </p>
  </div>

