  <h2 class="toc-group" id="density">Reading density</h2>

  <p>
    Two settings, chosen with the control in the header and remembered in
    <code>localStorage</code> under <code>usc-density</code>. Comfortable is the default.
    Compact moves three tokens — the reading size, the leading, and the space between
    paragraphs — and nothing else. The setting is stamped on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> before
    first paint by the same head script that stamps the theme, so a page never renders at one
    density and reflows to the other.
  </p>

  <p>
    <code>--measure</code> is a multiple of <code>--reading-size</code> rather than a fixed
    width, so the column narrows with the text and a compact page holds the same 62–70
    characters a line. <code>--indent-step</code> is in <code>ch</code> of the reading face, so
    the ladder narrows with it too. The readout below is the values in force right now.
  </p>

  <div class="spec">
    <table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless pairs" data-density-table>
